# Shared consumer-VPN egress ranges — matching addresses are capped at a
# ladder-max TEMP ban and can never become permanent or published.
#
# This is NOT an allowlist. Addresses here are still banned; they just cannot be
# banned FOREVER, because one address is shared by many unrelated people.
#
# Every line must be a real, narrow range with evidence. Lines broader than a
# /16 (v4) or /32 (v6) are rejected, and a rejected line fails the WHOLE file,
# turning the CIDR arm OFF.
#
# Note WHICH WAY that fails, because the earlier wording here had it backwards.
# Arm off means nothing is capped, so you get MORE permanent bans — including on
# the shared pools this file exists to protect. The floor guards the opposite
# hazard: an entry broad enough to match everyone would cap every perm and stop
# permanent banning altogether. Both are bad; they are not the same failure, and
# a rejected line causes the first, never the second.
104.28.0.0/16  # Cloudflare consumer WARP egress (1.1.1.1 app); NOT in the published CDN edge list
#
# Cloudflare consumer WARP IPv6 egress. RIPE registers this pool as eight
# discrete /32s, all netname CLOUDFLAREWARP; 2a09:bac8:: falls through to the
# parent 2a00::/11, so bac7 is the boundary. Verified 2026-08-13.
#
# Listed as eight /32s and deliberately NOT as the covering 2a09:bac0::/29:
# the floor above is a /32 for v6, so the /29 is rejected as over-broad — and a
# rejected line fails the WHOLE file, which turns the CIDR arm off and takes the
# IPv4 WARP line with it. Reproduced: with the /29 present, 104.28.196.52 stops
# matching. Same trap as any other over-broad entry; it just looks tidier.
2a09:bac0::/32  # Cloudflare consumer WARP egress (IPv6)
2a09:bac1::/32  # Cloudflare consumer WARP egress (IPv6)
2a09:bac2::/32  # Cloudflare consumer WARP egress (IPv6)
2a09:bac3::/32  # Cloudflare consumer WARP egress (IPv6)
2a09:bac4::/32  # Cloudflare consumer WARP egress (IPv6)
2a09:bac5::/32  # Cloudflare consumer WARP egress (IPv6)
2a09:bac6::/32  # Cloudflare consumer WARP egress (IPv6)
2a09:bac7::/32  # Cloudflare consumer WARP egress (IPv6)
